---
layout: _case_study
tags: []

title: Azuki Discover Screen
startDate: 2022
summary: Unified search and browse experience with sorting and filtering
role: Lead UX Designer
for: Azuki
goals:
  - Increase readership
  - Make it faster and easier to find a manga series

notes:
  -
    title: 'Problem: Similar User Goal'
    content: Search and browse serve a very similar purpose for users (finding manga), and user tests showed users trying both options to find something they were looking for (for example, searching for a genre in the search bar instead of using the filters on the browse screen).
  -
    title: 'Problem: Filter Interface Doesn’t Scale'
    content: The original filter interface takes up more space the more filter options it includes. This poses a problem as Azuki‘s manga library grows, especially on mobile devices where most of Azuki’s readership is.
  -
    title: Search and Discover Occupy Two Spots in the Nav Bar
    content: On mobile, nav bar space is highly limited. Taking up two spots for a similar user goal left less space for new features like the My Library tab that houses the user’s list and downloaded chapters.

phases:
  -
    title: Research
    items:
      - Studied search and browse screens on other manga apps (i.e. Shonen Jump) and non-manga media apps (i.e. Netflix)
      - Analyzed Google Analytics clickthrough metrics for the current search and browse interfaces
  -
    title: Exploration
    image:
      src: /images/projects/azuki-discover-exploration.jpg
      alt: ''
    items:
      - Created wireframes and rough mockups exploring adjustments to the current filter interface
      - Widened the exploration to more radical departures, including modal interfaces
      - Designs began with mobile, but eventually included desktop variants as well
  -
    title: Mockups
    image:
      src: /images/projects/azuki-discover-mockups.jpg
      alt: ''
    items:
      - Produced final, production-ready mockups for native mobile, mobile web, and desktop web
      - Handed off to iOS developer to build initial implementation
  -
    title: Results
    resultItems:
      -
        value: 17%
        label: increase in chapter reads generated by the search page

img:
